This getter is already a single array lookup, so there is little to gain. The rewrite binds the field entry to a reference and returns its flag. The compiler generates the same code either way, so expect no measurable speedup. Behavior is unchanged.

```cpp
FIT_BOOL Field::GetIsAccumulated() const
{
    const auto& fieldDef = profile->fields[profileIndex];
    return fieldDef.isAccumulated;
}
```